# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - GitOps Project Repository

This repository contains the applications and Kubernetes manifests for the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** project.

## Architecture

This project uses the **App-of-Apps** pattern. The central GitOps platform manages the root project application (`{{PROJECT_NAME}}-apps`), which monitors the `manifests/` folder in this repository:

- `manifests/kustomization.yaml`: Top-level Kustomize file discovering all child `Application` resources in this repository.
- `manifests/project.yaml`: ArgoCD `AppProject` definition isolating workloads to `{{PROJECT_NAME}}-*` namespaces.
- `manifests/<app>-app.yaml`: Child ArgoCD Application manifest for each microservice.
- `manifests/<app>/`: Kubernetes Deployment and Service definitions for each microservice.

## Adding a New Application / Microservice

To add a new microservice (e.g. `catalog`):
1. Create a directory `manifests/catalog/` containing your Kubernetes YAMLs (`deployment.yaml`, `service.yaml`, `kustomization.yaml`).
2. Add a child Application manifest `manifests/catalog-app.yaml`:
   ```yaml
   apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
   kind: Application
   metadata:
     name: catalog
     namespace: argocd
     labels:
       app.kubernetes.io/part-of: {{GITLAB_GROUP}}
       gitops.platform/group: {{GITLAB_GROUP}}
       gitops.platform/project: {{PROJECT_NAME}}
       gitops.platform/tier: workload
     finalizers:
       - resources-finalizer.argocd.argoproj.io
   spec:
     project: {{PROJECT_NAME}}
     source:
       repoURL: {{REPO_SSH_URL}}
       targetRevision: main
       path: manifests/catalog
     destination:
       server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
       namespace: catalog
     syncPolicy:
       syncOptions:
         - CreateNamespace=true
   ```
3. Add `catalog-app.yaml` to `manifests/kustomization.yaml`:
   ```yaml
   resources:
     - project.yaml
     - catalog-app.yaml
   ```
4. Commit and push via Merge Request to `main`! ArgoCD will automatically detect the new application and deploy it.
